  "details": "<p>W. Ball observes that this site begins as a circular fortification wall with towers that may surround a temple. Following destruction and abandonment, it was eventually reoccupied by mudbrick building of the Kushan period, Its final phase was as a wealthy house.</p>\r\n<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Jiga tepe, AFG</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A site located in Balkh Province, east of Dilbarjin. The material observed at the site dates to the Hellenistic, Kushan, and Early Sasanian periods.",
